From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:06:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(scoreboard): convert native sidebar title images and
 styled scores

Bedrock 1.26.51 resource packs can replace the objective title with a JSON UI image binding. Convert a bounded subset with literal title equality, a matching hidden label, explicit dimensions, and native sidebar anchors. Resolve active server UI and texture priority, isolate each image in its own font, and advertise authored dimensions for client integrations. Unsupported controls retain ordinary text.

Send objective CHANGE packets for repeated display titles without replacing score identities. Hide sidebar numbers while retaining score values for ordering, and send styled score display components separately from raw owners so extended Bedrock formatting survives. Other display slots keep numeric presentation. Invalidate older converted packs when the new metadata becomes available.

Saved protocol 2193 CubeCraft resources declare a 66 by 21 title image and 10-pixel player rows. The native Java 26.3 BlankFormat codec is registry zero with a unit payload. Targeted tests cover wire fields, pack priority, bounded UI parsing, image conversion, and disk cache rollover; captured resources remain private.

Read the bounded static sidebar parent image layout and texture nine-slice metadata. Carry authored alpha, content padding, and bottom-left row offsets into the converted resources. The saved CubeCraft protocol2193 pack declares Black_sb with 6 by 6 base size, two-pixel borders, .5 alpha, padding3/5 and row offsets2/-1. Preserve source pixels and reject unsupported transforms or expressions instead of activating an incorrect custom panel. Semantic conversion tests cover declared layout and fallback.

Read all 13 named material/coin/party variables alongside ordinary color variables from the target effective server UI globals. Bedrock 1.26.51.1/protocol2193 writer1403f9760 binds material_gold_color to the p table at1517f83c0 and party_blue_color to w at1517f8420. The saved Hive pack declares material gold as [.541,.824,.173], and the official Scallywag reference renders it green; ignoring named keys left Java gold. Keep immutable pack palettes in a neutral TextFormattingDefinitions shared by sidebar and player-name conversion. Preserve active styles across color codes not known by the dependency.

Advance the converted-pack identity after canonicalizing equipped
attachable selectors. Prior cache entries contain doubled variant names
and cannot safely serve the corrected item selection and worn renderer.

Advance the conversion identity after adding cutout-plane back faces so
existing disk caches cannot retain models with missing native geometry.
